  "turns": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Analyze the attached four-span continuous beam in OpenSees. Span lengths from left to right are 4, 6, 5 and 4 m, with supports S0/S1/S2/S3/S4 at global x=0/4/10/15/19 m, z=0. S0 is a pin; S1 through S4 are bilateral vertical rollers. All support rotations about Y are free, and every shared support node is continuous without member releases. Use material M1 throughout. Spans 1 and 4 use section B1; spans 2 and 3 use section B2, with the independent properties supplied. Case D applies -8 kN/m in global Z over the whole beam. Case L applies -10 kN/m in global Z only in spans 2 and 4. Define exactly C0=D and C1=1.2D+1.4L. Use first-order linear static Euler-Bernoulli analysis with self-weight disabled. For C0 and C1 separately, report all five vertical support reactions and all horizontal support reactions; signed uz at the four connected midpoint nodes P1/P2/P3/P4 (x=2/7/12.5/17 m); and signed local M2 on both sides of every internal support at x=4, 10 and 15 m. Identify each span, location, combination and unit.\n\nUse the complete attached input tables. Global XYZ is right handed with Z upward; any planar model uses the XZ plane. All nodes listed are connected physical joints. Member local x points from i to j. In 2D local y=global +Y and local z=x cross y. In 3D local y=normalize(reference cross x), local z=x cross y; reference vectors are explicit. N is positive in tension. Signed section N/T/M2/M3 equal minus the i-end resisting action at the start and plus the j-end action at the end; V2/V3 use plus i-end and minus j-end action. Report global nodal displacements and support reactions; rotations follow the right-hand rule. Distributed loads act per actual member length, including inclined members. Use first-order linear elasticity with self-weight, rigid floors, rigid offsets, P-delta and construction stages off. Use only the specified cases and combinations. Compute every request in output-requests.json, retaining its location, side, signed component, unit and case/combination. Interior forces must include applied-load terms. Execute OpenSees and retain version, runnable input, current-model hash, run ID, actual solver log and raw result/case mapping. Report the requested results in the response body as well as structured results; independently check equilibrium. No numerical answer or native execution evidence is supplied.",
      "state": 1,
      "expectation": "analyze",
      "attachments": [
        "geometry.json",
        "properties.json",
        "loads.json",
        "output-requests.json"
      ],
      "unresolvedFields": [],
      "expectedQuestions": []
    }
  ],
